speechtext:
1.	No.
2.	(a) He was absent from his office from July 7th to August 2nd inclusive;
(b)	On departmental business for 18 days;
(c)	To Halifax, Antigonish, Sydney and St. John.
3.	There is no regulation governing the annual vacation of deputy ministers. Hitherto the Deputy Minister of Marine has not been in the habit of taking regular annual vacations. During many of the years of his incumbency he has not taken any vacation. On one occasion only he took a vacation on account of ill-health extending over a period of about four weeks.
4.	There is no record of the time he has been absent from his office since his appointment.
